#Service
=======

A Kubernetes Service provides a stable IP address and DNS name to access a group of Pods, even when Pod IP addresses change.

$ kubectl get svc

=====================
2. Types of Services
====================

1. ClusterIP Service: 

    Default Service type.
    Used for internal communication within the Kubernetes cluster.
    Not directly accessible from outside the cluster.

2. NodePort Service: 

    Exposes an application through a port on each Kubernetes node.
    Can be accessed externally using Node IP and NodePort, provided network access is configured.
    Default NodePort range: 30000–32767.

3. Loadbalancer: 

    Exposes an application through a cloud provider load balancer.
    

